# PhiTeX Instant @VERSION@: building the packages from source

This archive holds the add-on's source and the PhiTeX engine it embeds:

- the top level: PhiTeX-frontends at commit @FRONTENDS@
  (https://github.com/accl-kaust/PhiTeX-frontends);
- `phitex/`: PhiTeX at commit @PHITEX@, the frontends' submodule
  (https://github.com/accl-kaust/PhiTeX).

Keep the layout: the build reads the engine from `phitex/`.

## What is built, and from what

| In the package | Built from |
| --- | --- |
| `dist/*.js`, `dist/common/**/*.js` | `apps/overleaf/src/**/*.ts`, `common/src/**/*.ts` and PhiTeX's `phitex/viewer/src/*.ts`, by esbuild (bundled, **not minified**) |
| `dist/core.wasm`, `dist/core1.wasm` | `phitex/crates/wasm/live` (Rust), by `phitex/scripts/wasm-live.sh`: `wasm32-wasip1-threads` and `wasm32-wasip1` |
| `dist/diff.wasm` | `phitex/crates/wasm/diff` (Compare's latexdiff), by the same script, `wasm32-unknown-unknown` |
| `formats/*.fmt.gzdata` | made by `core1.wasm` itself (`tools/build/make-formats.sh`) from TeX Live 2026 files: pdfLaTeX, XeLaTeX, plain TeX, plain XeTeX |
| `texmf/` | TeX Live 2026 files, from TeX Live's package archive (`tools/build/fetch-texmf.sh`, into `shelf/texmf/`) |
| `packs/` | the list of packages fetched in the background (`tools/build/bundle-packs.sh`) |
| `shelf-*.gzdata`, `shelf-release.json` | Shelf's index and pack table for release tl2026.9 (`shelf/`) |
| `dist/pyodide/` | the npm package `pyodide@@PYODIDE@`, unmodified (`python_stdlib.zip` renamed `python_stdlib.data`) |
| `minted/*.whl.data` | TeX Live 2026's wheels in `texmf-dist/scripts/minted/`, renamed |
| `dist/minted/runner.mjs` | `phitex/tools/minted-pyodide/runner.mjs`, as is |
| `fonts/` | Latin Modern, the fonts the pages are drawn in (`common/fonts`, from TeX Live 2026; GUST Font License) |

Some files are renamed `.data` or `.gzdata` because Edge's store refuses a
package with archives inside. Their contents are unchanged, and the code
reads them by those names.

## Requirements

- Linux x86_64 with bubblewrap (`bwrap`): every step runs in
  `tools/sandbox`, which has no network unless `--net` is given.
- Rust `nightly-2026-08-08` (`phitex/rust-toolchain.toml`) with the
  targets the cores need:

      rustup target add wasm32-wasip1-threads wasm32-wasip1 wasm32-unknown-unknown --toolchain nightly-2026-08-08

- Node.js 22 or later, and npm.
- TeX Live 2026 under `/usr/share/texmf-dist` (it provides the formats'
  sources, the fonts and the minted wheels).
- python3, zip, unzip, gzip.

## Steps

    tools/sandbox --net npm ci --ignore-scripts     # esbuild, TypeScript, pdfjs-dist, pyodide (package-lock.json)
    tools/sandbox --net tools/build/fetch-texmf.sh  # shelf/texmf/ from TeX Live's package archive
    tools/build/package.sh                          # → build/phitex-instant-@VERSION@.zip (Chrome, Edge)
                                                    #   build/phitex-instant-@VERSION@-firefox.zip (Firefox)

`tools/build/package.sh` runs `tools/build/build.sh`: the wasm cores
(cargo, a few minutes: fat LTO), the formats made and then checked by both
cores, the bundled TeX files, the esbuild bundles and the vendored npm
files. Then it zips the Firefox package, whose manifest differs from
Chrome's: a background page (`firefox-bg.html`) instead of a service
worker, and `browser_specific_settings`.

The cores in the store packages were built from this archive's `phitex/`, by
the frontends' release workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`), with the
steps above.
A rebuild here makes the same code; the `.wasm` bytes can differ by
machine paths in debug sections.

## Notes for reviewers

- **No remote code.** All JavaScript and WebAssembly is in the package.
  At run time the add-on downloads only TeX Live data files (packs) and
  Shelf's index of them, from `v1.shelf.phitex.org` (else
  `shelf-phitex-v1.pages.dev`), by package name. It never sends document
  content.
- **Dynamic code:** `eval` and `import()` with computed paths are inside
  Pyodide and pdf.js, vendored unmodified. The add-on's own dynamic imports
  load files from the package (`new URL(..., import.meta.url)`).
- **HTML:** the panel builds its UI from fixed templates (`html\`\``,
  `apps/overleaf/src/dom.ts` and `phitex/viewer/src/html.ts`); text from a
  document or a diagnostic is inserted as text, never as markup.
- License: AGPL-3.0-only (`LICENSE`). Bundled components keep their own
  licenses (`NOTICE`).
